Ticket **#4471** merged 412 unique reports (427 export rows; 15 duplicate ids) and marked them known as one month-flip bug. The desk’s own cause logic disagrees: **two** causes sit in that merge.

<Callout>
Not one issue. `parser` owns most of the queue; `hint` has no ticket of its own.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets filed

| cause | reports | public ticket |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | https://github.com/novumhouse/mega.voicetta/issues/1 |
| `hint` | 33 | https://github.com/novumhouse/mega.voicetta/issues/2 |

- **`parser`:** the shared parser reads month first; day-first tenants flip.
- **`hint`:** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`; day-first tenants type that order; the form still reads day first. Tenants: `alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, `pale.harbour`. Form channel only.

Subject-line dedupe ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) hid the split. Match on cause (tenant locale + channel + form), not on subject alone.

## Desk notes

Five reports in `desk-notes.json` (`oneDayMove`) were read as a one-day move. They stay under `parser` by tenant in this table; they are not a third cause in `causes.ts`.

